# Direct Single-Input Answers Under Five Seconds

Status: DONE
Milestone: Q3 Measured answer usefulness and latency
Dependencies: 39_INSTALLED_CLI_ANSWERS.todo

## Purpose

Answer the submitted question directly instead of returning coding-agent workspace plans, with measured latency.

## Tasks

- [x] Add a fixed answer-only policy; question remains exact data, no file/tool inspection.
- [x] Make reasonable assumptions/default language instead of requesting another input.
- [x] Reuse a supported prepared transport while creating a fresh isolated context for each question.
- [x] Prepare one empty fresh session without model prompts and show cold preparation distinctly from answer time.
- [x] Select a measured suitable model/profile, retaining explicit configuration and no fallback.
- [x] Iterate controlled synthetic trials for COMPLETE useful responses under5000ms; retain every result.
- [x] Keep permission/tool requests denied, bounded deadlines, cancellation, no auto-resend and fresh request IDs.
- [x] Record cold/warm, first text, full text, terminal and cleanup times in local diagnostics.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] The provided Two Sum intent produces a correct usable solution, not directory commands.
- [x] One prompt is the only user input; no follow-up, permission or authentication wait is treated as progress.
- [x] No first-token/filler or truncated answer is substituted for the under-five-second target.
- [x] If a target is not achieved consistently, its failures and external limits remain explicit.

